    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0145" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1136</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-23T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 23,
                                1918, 8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 21, 4 p.m., February 23, 4 p.m., and February 23, 5 p.m. The
                    attitude of the American Government is stated in a telegram of February 13, 7
                        p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d81-f1"/> to Tokyo which has already been
                    repeated to you. You will communicate orally to the Foreign Office the views
                    expressed therein.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
